WEBVTT

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:30.820
Yes, you should wash it inside out.

00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:33.110
Thank you very much!

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:40.120
It's a hot one today.

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:44.710
I wonder if Asumi and Minato
are doing their best?

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:51.420
It's been one month of water polo,

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:56.590
and for Golden Week, we're having
a training camp at school.

00:00:56.590 --> 00:01:01.180
"Get 1st Win"

00:00:56.590 --> 00:01:01.180
We're aiming for our first win
at July prefecturals.

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:05.390
"Get 1st Win"

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:05.390
Obviously, our ultimate goal
is to be the champs,

00:01:05.390 --> 00:01:11.400
so we stopped building strategies
around me and tried something new.

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:16.950
I've become the passer.
So if Amihama outswims his defender...

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:20.780
...I pass... and he shoots.

00:01:22.490 --> 00:01:26.290
If Ejiri manages to get open...

00:01:26.290 --> 00:01:28.120
He shoots.

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:30.590
Hell yeah!

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:34.590
I'm feeling good about this strategy!

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:36.760
All right! Take a break!

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:38.550
Okay!

00:01:46.390 --> 00:01:48.980
Nice! I'm getting all of it!

00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:52.900
I sunk most my money
into buying this phone.

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:57.280
It's to study myself
"like the old me did."

00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:01.200
"Like the old me did"

00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:01.200
to become a great player.

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:03.620
He's smiling again.

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:06.750
What a narcissist.

00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:12.040
No, wait! I'm smiling at my new phone,
not from seeing myself.

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:13.960
Eh?

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:14.710
Shady.

00:02:14.710 --> 00:02:16.130
Shady.

00:02:16.130 --> 00:02:17.050
It is.

00:02:17.050 --> 00:02:18.300
For real!

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:19.720
Eh?

00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:23.140
Why are you leaning like that? Cut it out!

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:24.390
Eh?!

00:02:24.390 --> 00:02:26.770
Cut it out!

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:32.110
Anyway, we were finally
feeling good about things...

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:43.410
I hate this...

00:04:14.290 --> 00:04:16.920
"Episode 6: Hey! Look this way!"

00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:20.300
"Episode 6: Hey! Look this way!"
It's dang cold!

00:04:23.130 --> 00:04:26.850
Huh? What? What the--?!

00:04:28.930 --> 00:04:30.640
The choices!

00:04:30.640 --> 00:04:34.060
Here! Thank you!

00:04:34.060 --> 00:04:35.850
--Mmm!
--Tasty!

00:04:35.850 --> 00:04:39.900
--It's so good!
--Tastes better when you're tired!

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:49.700
Gimme a sec! Hmm, what to say?
Let's see... Um...

00:04:49.700 --> 00:04:51.700
"Chitose Rental Futons"

00:04:49.700 --> 00:04:51.700
Gimme a sec! Hmm, what to say?
Let's see... Um...

00:04:51.700 --> 00:04:54.210
"A.M."
"P.M."
Gimme a sec! Hmm, what to say?
Let's see... Um...

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:57.580
"Let's do our best!"

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:57.580
You've got that many confessions?

00:04:57.580 --> 00:05:00.170
Huh? Just one is good, right?

00:05:00.170 --> 00:05:02.460
That's standard.

00:05:03.880 --> 00:05:09.100
Then... In my head, I call Ejiri "Buu!"

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:10.140
Huh?!

00:05:10.140 --> 00:05:11.510
Buu?

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:12.220
'Cuz if you read his name like it's
a long vowel instead, it's "Buu."

00:05:12.220 --> 00:05:15.980
"Takekazu Ejiri"
'Cuz if you read his name like it's
a long vowel instead, it's "Buu."

00:05:15.980 --> 00:05:17.020
"Buu Ejiri"
'Cuz if you read his name like it's
a long vowel instead, it's "Buu."

00:05:17.020 --> 00:05:18.400
Ridiculous!

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:20.360
Still, "Buu" is cute!

00:05:20.360 --> 00:05:21.320
Mm-hmm.

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:25.110
Huh?! Don't you dare!
I hate that nickname!

00:05:25.110 --> 00:05:26.490
And why's that?

00:05:26.490 --> 00:05:28.530
It's just so lame!

00:05:28.530 --> 00:05:30.490
Eh?

00:05:30.490 --> 00:05:34.450
Hey! Don't go stealing the lean, pal!

00:05:35.660 --> 00:05:37.330
Now it's my turn.

00:05:37.330 --> 00:05:38.830
Huh?

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:42.340
G-Go ahead.

00:05:42.340 --> 00:05:48.130
One of my confessions...
is that my parents are divorced.

00:05:48.130 --> 00:05:54.640
My brother and I have different last names
because my dad was an adopted son-in-law.

00:05:54.640 --> 00:05:57.060
Well, that's no fun.

00:05:57.060 --> 00:05:58.440
Mm-hmm.

00:05:58.440 --> 00:06:01.020
That went in a different direction.

00:06:01.020 --> 00:06:03.110
Talk about "heavy."

00:06:03.110 --> 00:06:07.110
Was it? To me, it's not a big deal.

00:06:07.110 --> 00:06:09.030
Good, I guess.

00:06:09.030 --> 00:06:12.620
Um... You're next, Minato-<i>senpai</i>.

00:06:12.620 --> 00:06:14.160
Right.

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:20.210
Um, my confession... is about my memories.

00:06:21.290 --> 00:06:24.840
Oh, it's not that they're
back or anything.

00:06:24.840 --> 00:06:29.130
It's more about my feelings right now.

00:06:29.130 --> 00:06:33.560
Obviously, I want my
memories to come back.

00:06:33.560 --> 00:06:37.230
But I'm also scared for them to.

00:06:39.020 --> 00:06:40.650
Scared?

00:06:40.650 --> 00:06:48.490
In dramas, when someone has amnesia
and finally regains their memories,

00:06:48.490 --> 00:06:54.160
they forget the people and memories
they made in the meantime.

00:06:54.160 --> 00:06:58.750
Thinking that could happen... scares me.

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:03.170
So it could, then?

00:07:03.170 --> 00:07:04.500
Not really.

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:05.420
Huh?

00:07:05.420 --> 00:07:06.670
--Eh?
--Huh?

00:07:06.670 --> 00:07:13.930
The doctor said if my memories come back,
it won't erase any new ones.

00:07:13.930 --> 00:07:16.310
But I thought, what if?

00:07:16.310 --> 00:07:21.100
The hell--?! So you're scared for nothing?

00:07:21.100 --> 00:07:22.350
Yeah.

00:07:22.350 --> 00:07:24.610
You scared us!

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:25.940
Thank goodness.

00:07:25.940 --> 00:07:28.110
--Yeah.
--Mmm.

00:07:28.110 --> 00:07:32.740
Deep down, I know it won't happen, but...

00:07:32.740 --> 00:07:39.250
...the thought of losing my memories
of you guys... it's awful.

00:07:44.710 --> 00:07:48.250
We're finally getting along together.

00:07:53.050 --> 00:07:58.100
I know it won't happen,
and I'm an idiot for worrying,

00:07:58.100 --> 00:08:03.980
but it's a weight off my shoulders,
so I'm glad I told you guys.

00:08:07.940 --> 00:08:10.030
We are, too.

00:08:10.030 --> 00:08:11.530
--Yeah.
--Mmm.

00:08:11.530 --> 00:08:13.070
--Mmm.
--Mmm.

00:08:14.070 --> 00:08:17.990
Uh, then our last confession is... Ushi!

00:08:17.990 --> 00:08:21.040
Huh? I don't have one.

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:22.460
No fair!

00:08:22.460 --> 00:08:23.670
It's true.

00:08:23.670 --> 00:08:27.460
I even said where I keep my bankbook!

00:08:27.460 --> 00:08:29.750
We didn't wanna know.

00:08:29.750 --> 00:08:33.300
Huh? But that's a huge secret!

00:08:43.350 --> 00:08:45.480
It's still early.

00:08:54.990 --> 00:08:56.240
Huh?

00:09:12.300 --> 00:09:16.340
Basically, we do the same
routine every day.

00:09:17.590 --> 00:09:23.020
In the morning, we swim--
eight kilometers over three hours.

00:09:30.190 --> 00:09:35.700
We start water polo training in
the afternoon, but no balls yet.

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:39.070
We do eggbeaters with weights...

00:09:39.070 --> 00:09:40.620
Jumping...

00:09:46.040 --> 00:09:53.880
At last, we break out the ball practice.
From normal passes to long passing...

00:09:56.050 --> 00:09:59.180
And after that, shooting!

00:10:01.970 --> 00:10:04.430
Here it comes!

00:10:17.780 --> 00:10:21.280
It's nothing to worry about, but ice it.

00:10:21.280 --> 00:10:22.330
Got it.

00:10:22.330 --> 00:10:27.410
It'll hurt, but once the pain subsides,
it won't hurt anymore.

00:10:27.410 --> 00:10:29.370
Obviously.

00:10:29.370 --> 00:10:31.880
Mitamura-<i>sensei</i>! We're done running.

00:10:31.880 --> 00:10:37.340
Yeah, okay. I'll be at the gym,
so go to the gym if you need me.

00:10:37.340 --> 00:10:38.840
Right.

00:10:40.840 --> 00:10:42.140
That's...!

00:10:42.140 --> 00:10:42.890
Hmm?

00:10:42.890 --> 00:10:44.470
It's nothing.

00:10:53.770 --> 00:10:55.610
What an odd advisor.

00:10:55.610 --> 00:10:58.070
Don't say that.

00:10:58.070 --> 00:11:03.870
When nobody would be our advisor,
Mitamura took on a second club.

00:11:03.870 --> 00:11:07.870
You okay, Ushi? Sorry for drilling you.

00:11:07.870 --> 00:11:10.420
No, it's my fault.

00:11:10.420 --> 00:11:14.090
Yeah. You were completely zoned out.

00:11:15.050 --> 00:11:16.920
Sorry.

00:11:16.920 --> 00:11:18.970
From lack of sleep?

00:11:18.970 --> 00:11:20.180
Huh?

00:11:20.180 --> 00:11:22.680
You weren't in bed this morning.

00:11:22.680 --> 00:11:24.180
--What?
--Huh?

00:11:24.180 --> 00:11:26.060
Where were you?

00:11:30.480 --> 00:11:31.980
Running.

00:11:31.980 --> 00:11:33.770
--What?
--Huh?

00:11:33.770 --> 00:11:37.440
I wanna build up my endurance.

00:11:40.860 --> 00:11:42.950
But why do that?

00:11:42.950 --> 00:11:49.290
'Cuz I only drag everyone down.
I'm worthless at shooting...

00:11:49.290 --> 00:11:52.830
My long passes don't reach...

00:11:52.830 --> 00:11:56.340
I'm the only one who sinks...

00:11:56.340 --> 00:12:02.550
Everyone's getting better
but me... It's pathetic.

00:12:02.550 --> 00:12:04.300
Nah, you're not holding us--

00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:06.260
I am!

00:12:08.010 --> 00:12:13.770
I think we need to relax.
Take a minute to cool down?

00:12:15.190 --> 00:12:16.650
Okay.

00:12:16.060 --> 00:12:20.070
"Let's do our best!"

00:12:18.570 --> 00:12:23.410
I'm worried. He really thinks
he's dragging us down.

00:12:23.410 --> 00:12:27.280
I doubt he'll believe anything we say.

00:12:27.280 --> 00:12:29.740
What to do...

00:12:34.210 --> 00:12:37.210
"Let's do our best!"

00:12:37.210 --> 00:12:40.170
"Kawabe JH"

00:12:43.340 --> 00:12:45.890
--Hey, that's mine!
--You said I could look!

00:12:45.890 --> 00:12:49.430
What the hell?! Hey, come back!

00:12:54.020 --> 00:12:58.110
I'm so disgusted with myself.

00:13:00.650 --> 00:13:03.740
Um, what about shooting practice?

00:13:03.740 --> 00:13:08.620
I'll jump in the opposite direction
so his shot goes in.

00:13:08.620 --> 00:13:10.490
And for eggbeater?

00:13:10.490 --> 00:13:18.420
While I'm distracting Ushi, Eitaro will
swap his ten-kilo weight for five kilos.

00:13:18.420 --> 00:13:21.210
He'll be able to stay afloat!

00:13:21.210 --> 00:13:23.300
What about long passing?

00:13:23.300 --> 00:13:26.630
We'll start off closer than we usually do.

00:13:26.630 --> 00:13:33.310
Then, when Ushi throws his pass, I'll move
a bit forward so it makes it to me.

00:13:33.310 --> 00:13:36.350
Perfect!

00:13:36.350 --> 00:13:38.100
Let's give it a shot?

00:13:38.100 --> 00:13:39.440
Yeah!

00:13:45.320 --> 00:13:48.200
Hey, does it still hurt?

00:13:49.320 --> 00:13:51.410
Huh?

00:13:51.410 --> 00:13:53.040
The toilet?

00:13:53.040 --> 00:13:55.120
Hey, look.

00:13:55.120 --> 00:13:58.630
"Sorry, everyone"

00:13:58.920 --> 00:14:01.840
Is that Ushimado's?

00:14:01.840 --> 00:14:04.050
Oh, no...

00:14:04.050 --> 00:14:08.130
Ushi and I talk on our way home...

00:14:09.140 --> 00:14:16.020
In junior high, he had no friends and
thought, "There's no value in me living."

00:14:17.140 --> 00:14:22.020
"But I don't think that way anymore
'cuz I've got you guys."

00:14:22.020 --> 00:14:25.780
But if he thinks he's worthless again...

00:14:30.160 --> 00:14:32.780
Ushimado!

00:14:34.450 --> 00:14:36.870
Ushi!

00:14:40.580 --> 00:14:43.960
Hey! Where are you?!

00:14:43.960 --> 00:14:46.380
Ushi!

00:14:48.340 --> 00:14:51.640
Hey! Ushi!

00:14:55.270 --> 00:14:57.310
Don't!

00:14:59.230 --> 00:15:00.350
Ow!

00:15:00.350 --> 00:15:04.020
What are you doing, man?! You can't!

00:15:04.020 --> 00:15:06.280
H-Huh? What?

00:15:06.280 --> 00:15:09.780
You were gonna hang yourself! Uh...

00:15:11.360 --> 00:15:12.320
Huh?

00:15:12.320 --> 00:15:15.950
The clothesline for drying fell down.

00:15:15.950 --> 00:15:18.540
Oh...

00:15:18.540 --> 00:15:21.420
Then, the chalkboard...?

00:15:21.420 --> 00:15:26.000
I'm bad at communicating,
but I wanted to say sorry.

00:15:26.000 --> 00:15:27.210
Oh!

00:15:27.210 --> 00:15:28.800
The hell, Babi?!

00:15:28.800 --> 00:15:30.180
Sorry!

00:15:30.180 --> 00:15:32.640
Why come to the pool?

00:15:32.640 --> 00:15:35.350
To practice, since I feel better.

00:15:35.350 --> 00:15:40.270
Ooh, I see! Is everyone
ready to get started?

00:15:40.270 --> 00:15:41.730
Yeah!

00:15:41.730 --> 00:15:46.690
Let's do it! Go get changed
and we'll practice shooting!

00:15:46.690 --> 00:15:50.450
You're really going to boost
his ego with lies?

00:15:50.450 --> 00:15:51.360
--Huh?
--Uh...

00:15:51.360 --> 00:15:52.860
Lies?

00:15:52.860 --> 00:15:59.660
Yeah. They're gonna go easy on you
to help out your confidence.

00:15:59.660 --> 00:16:00.660
Really?

00:16:00.660 --> 00:16:02.370
N-No!

00:16:02.370 --> 00:16:05.040
Hey! What are you saying?!

00:16:05.040 --> 00:16:06.540
The truth.

00:16:06.540 --> 00:16:08.800
Why are you blowing it?!

00:16:08.800 --> 00:16:15.510
Because I'm against it.
What you're doing won't help Ushimado.

00:16:16.890 --> 00:16:20.270
Okay! Let's break it up.

00:16:22.350 --> 00:16:27.020
Everyone... I have a confession to make.

00:16:27.020 --> 00:16:28.110
--Eh?
--Huh?

00:16:28.110 --> 00:16:30.190
What is it?

00:16:30.190 --> 00:16:34.990
To be honest, I didn't join
water polo 'cuz I wanted to.

00:16:34.990 --> 00:16:36.700
--Huh?
--What?

00:16:36.700 --> 00:16:41.500
The day after I transferred,
there were printouts on our desks.

00:16:41.500 --> 00:16:42.830
Oh, that?

00:16:42.830 --> 00:16:44.000
Mine?!

00:16:44.000 --> 00:16:49.630
"Hey Dudes!!"

00:16:44.000 --> 00:16:49.630
One of the loud students took it and said,
"Who the hell plays water polo?"

00:16:49.630 --> 00:16:51.130
One of the loud students took it and said,
"Who the hell plays water polo?"

00:16:51.130 --> 00:16:54.010
Dude, someone join as a joke!

00:16:54.010 --> 00:16:55.010
No way.

00:16:55.010 --> 00:16:57.430
Ain't happening!

00:16:57.430 --> 00:16:59.220
How about you?

00:17:01.140 --> 00:17:03.690
Wouldn't it be funny if he did it?

00:17:03.690 --> 00:17:05.440
No, but I...

00:17:05.440 --> 00:17:09.070
Aww! Not gonna join?

00:17:09.070 --> 00:17:18.070
Afraid I'd end up without any friends
like in junior high, I couldn't refuse.

00:17:20.790 --> 00:17:25.250
But now, I'm actually glad
I joined this club.

00:17:25.250 --> 00:17:30.750
You were gonna trick me to give
me confidence... or try to stop it.

00:17:30.750 --> 00:17:35.880
You're teammates who cry at
the thought of forgetting me...

00:17:37.390 --> 00:17:42.970
I wanna get good and not drag you down,
but I won't be so hard on myself.

00:17:42.970 --> 00:17:46.600
I'll work hard without worrying you guys.

00:17:48.060 --> 00:17:54.820
You can talk after all, Ushi!
I've never heard your voice this much.

00:17:54.820 --> 00:17:57.070
That's it!

00:17:57.070 --> 00:18:00.370
Ushimado, can you get in the pool?

00:18:09.290 --> 00:18:11.380
Senpai, will this really--?

00:18:11.380 --> 00:18:13.550
It's gonna work!

00:18:26.690 --> 00:18:29.770
Whoa! Did you see that speed?!

00:18:29.770 --> 00:18:32.070
Yeah! It felt different!

00:18:32.070 --> 00:18:35.650
Well? Don't you feel stronger by shouting?

00:18:36.780 --> 00:18:40.240
I realized you were silent when we played!

00:18:40.240 --> 00:18:45.250
If you shout, you get more power
when you shoot or jump!

00:18:45.250 --> 00:18:47.660
I see.

00:18:47.660 --> 00:18:51.710
C'mon! Give us another Ushimado Shout!

00:18:51.710 --> 00:18:54.920
"Ushimado Shout"?

00:18:54.920 --> 00:18:56.260
Right.

00:19:07.140 --> 00:19:08.180
I did it!

00:19:08.180 --> 00:19:10.690
--Hell yeah!
--Woo-hoo!

00:19:16.650 --> 00:19:19.320
Hey! Look this way!

00:19:22.990 --> 00:19:26.660
Woo-hoo!

00:19:26.660 --> 00:19:30.620
--Way to go, Ushimado!
--Don't drown him!

00:19:33.340 --> 00:19:36.340
"2 Days Later"

00:19:36.710 --> 00:19:38.210
Hawaii! No fair!

00:19:38.210 --> 00:19:39.670
You go anywhere?

00:19:39.670 --> 00:19:41.720
Yeah, but in Japan!

00:19:41.720 --> 00:19:43.010
Hey.

00:19:46.310 --> 00:19:49.350
You're still doing water polo?

00:19:51.140 --> 00:19:52.150
Yeah.

00:19:52.150 --> 00:19:56.150
If you don't want to, just quit.

00:19:56.150 --> 00:19:57.900
I won't.

00:19:59.190 --> 00:20:01.450
I wanna play.

00:20:03.110 --> 00:20:04.910
All right.

00:20:12.120 --> 00:20:14.420
Sorry to bother you.

00:20:14.420 --> 00:20:16.710
It's no big deal.

00:20:16.710 --> 00:20:18.760
I've got something to say.

00:20:18.760 --> 00:20:20.090
Huh?

00:20:20.090 --> 00:20:23.300
I love water polo.

00:20:23.300 --> 00:20:29.310
I started 'cuz I couldn't pay you back,
but now I'm loving it.

00:20:29.310 --> 00:20:32.690
Thanks for telling me our promise.

00:20:33.900 --> 00:20:35.270
Yeah.

00:20:35.270 --> 00:20:39.230
So, you knew Okayama's best
meant Japan's best?

00:20:39.230 --> 00:20:40.030
Uh...

00:20:40.030 --> 00:20:44.450
'Cuz Shogakukan in Okayama
is the best in Japan.

00:20:44.450 --> 00:20:51.000
You got me. I thought you'd never
agree if I said "Japan's best."

00:20:54.580 --> 00:21:00.050
Still, I think I'm gonna aim to be
Japan's best after all. See ya!

00:21:04.300 --> 00:21:09.930
Since it's our last day, let's talk
about July 18th's prefecturals!

00:21:09.930 --> 00:21:17.360
This year, it's a round-robin with Rikka
and Shogaku! Three games in one day!

00:21:17.360 --> 00:21:18.770
Eh?

00:21:18.770 --> 00:21:20.480
So, we play twice?

00:21:20.480 --> 00:21:23.700
First is versus Rikka,
which means the second...

00:21:23.700 --> 00:21:28.120
You're kidding! We have to face
Shogaku while exhausted?

00:21:28.120 --> 00:21:35.540
However! They play Rikka after we do,
so they'll be more tired for our match!

00:21:35.540 --> 00:21:41.050
Well, they actually train
to handle multiple games.

00:21:43.170 --> 00:21:46.720
All right! Lez do this!

00:21:58.610 --> 00:22:05.450
<i>I'm not gonna regret it</i>

00:22:05.450 --> 00:22:11.240
<i>I honestly won't</i>

00:22:12.240 --> 00:22:19.000
<i>The stairs to that dear future</i>

00:22:19.000 --> 00:22:27.130
<i>Are crumbling down</i>

00:22:27.130 --> 00:22:31.550
<i>Just who are they</i>

00:22:33.890 --> 00:22:39.020
<i>There's a me just like me at my side</i>

00:22:39.020 --> 00:22:42.020
<i>Laughing</i>

00:22:46.280 --> 00:22:49.610
<i>All the many sights and</i>

00:22:49.610 --> 00:22:53.080
<i>All the words you left behind</i>

00:22:53.080 --> 00:22:59.870
<i>Are looking a little warped</i>

00:22:59.870 --> 00:23:03.290
<i>Someone, anyone tell me</i>

00:23:03.290 --> 00:23:06.260
<i>It hurts, it hurts, it hurts</i>

00:23:06.260 --> 00:23:14.600
<i>What am I suddenly crying for?</i>
